## 🔴 Bug 1 — [maybe_request_flip](file:///c:/Users/brock/Downloads/303-main/303-main/main.py#4191-4283) calls [early_sell_profit_gate](file:///c:/Users/brock/Downloads/303-main/303-main/main.py#392-451) with wrong defaults

**[main.py:4241-4245](file:///c:/Users/brock/Downloads/303-main/303-main/main.py#L4241-L4245)**

```python
flip_ok, net_bid, req_bid = early_sell_profit_gate(
    sec_remaining=T_sec,
    bid=sell_bid,
    entry_price=sell_entry,
)
```

Missing `p_cone`, [side](file:///c:/Users/brock/Downloads/303-main/303-main/main.py#933-936), and `T_entry`. Defaults to `p_cone=0.5`, `side="UP"`, `T_entry=0.0`:

- **If flipping from DOWN→UP**, `p_side` uses `p_cone` directly instead of `1-p_cone` → **wrong exit target**, potentially blocking profitable flips or allowing unprofitable ones.
- `T_entry=0.0` falls back to `230.0` internally — benign but imprecise.

**Fix:**
```python
flip_ok, net_bid, req_bid = early_sell_profit_gate(
    sec_remaining=T_sec,
    bid=sell_bid,
    entry_price=sell_entry,
    p_cone=float(p_cone),
    side=cur_side,
    T_entry=max(1.0, 300.0 - T_sec),
)
```

