## 🔴 Bug 2 — Flow tracker biased by unknown trade sides

**[main.py:3171-3172](file:///c:/Users/brock/Downloads/303-main/303-main/main.py#L3171-L3172)**

```python
side = msg.get("side")
is_buy = True if side == "BUY" else False
```

When [side](file:///c:/Users/brock/Downloads/303-main/303-main/main.py#933-936) is `None` (no field in message), `is_buy = False`. Every unknown-side trade is recorded as a **sell** in `FLOW.record_fill()`.

**Impact:**
- Biases `FLOW.imbalance()` toward negative (sell-heavy)
- Can trigger incorrect `FLOW_ADVERSE_GATE` blocks on UP entries
- Affects `flow_reversal` exit logic (line 4809)
- Affects flow-weighted sizing via `_flow_sz_scale`

**Fix:**
```python
side = msg.get("side")
if side is None:
    return  # skip flow recording for ambiguous trades
is_buy = (side == "BUY")
```

