## 🟡 Bug 4 — [survival_decide_portfolio](file:///c:/Users/brock/Downloads/303-main/303-main/main.py#4069-4189) only exits one leg at expiry

**[main.py:4114-4125](file:///c:/Users/brock/Downloads/303-main/303-main/main.py#L4114-L4125)**

When holding **both** UP and DOWN with ≤8s left, only UP is exited (first branch). DOWN only triggers if UP is zero or bookless. In a straddle, the DOWN leg wastes precious seconds.

**Fix:** Prioritize larger leg:
```python
if sec_remaining <= 8:
    legs = []
    if A > 0 and bid_up > 0.01:
        legs.append(("UP", UP_TOKEN_ID, A, bid_up))
    if B > 0 and bid_dn > 0.01:
        legs.append(("DOWN", DOWN_TOKEN_ID, B, bid_dn))
    if legs:
        legs.sort(key=lambda x: x[2], reverse=True)
        side, tid, qty, bid = legs[0]
        return {"action": "EXIT", "reason": "last_8s", ...}
```

